                <pb facs="0546" n="444" xml:id="pg444"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2126/351.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Furniss.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-12-07"><hi rendition="#italic">December 7,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Bacon informs Mr. Furniss that the supplementary telegram of December 5 was
                    not intended to limit the good offices of the United States to Europeans, as
                    temporary protection will be cheerfully extended as far as practicable to
                    citizens of any friendly State not having naval vessels at hand. Mr. Furniss is
                    instructed to show this to the senior American naval officer.</p>
            </div>
